Subject: SystemdSysupdateBackend: report error replies instead of taking them for versions

GetVersion and CheckNew were read straight into a QString, and an error
reply converts to its own message, so a refused check ("Interactive
authentication required") became an update to a version of that name.
Each reply is now checked: an error is shown as a passive message and the
target gets no resource. A failed ListTargets ends the fetch it began, so
the backend does not stay busy.

installApplication set needsReboot before the transaction ran, so a refused
or failed Acquire still left "A pending update will be installed when
restarting". The flag is now set when the Install job ends with status 0.

The update size is asked of http://localhost:3129 once per resource; when
nothing answers, the size stays 0 and sizeDescription() is empty, which
hides the page's size row instead of spinning a busy indicator for ever.

diff --git a/libdiscover/backends/SystemdSysupdateBackend/SystemdSysupdateBackend.cpp b/libdiscover/backends/SystemdSysupdateBackend/SystemdSysupdateBackend.cpp
index 77325f7..00120f1 100644
